# 4. Template Usage Rules

## Purpose

This section establishes the rules governing the use of the Objective Template throughout the Adaptive Vehicle Intelligence Architecture (AVIA) repository.

Its purpose is to ensure that all System Objectives are created, maintained, and revised in a consistent and controlled manner.

---

## Usage Rules

### TUR-01 — Mandatory Use

Every approved System Objective shall be documented using this template.

No alternative document structure shall be used unless formally approved through the AVIA governance process.

---

### TUR-02 — Structural Integrity

The mandatory sections of this template shall not be removed, renamed, or reordered without formal governance approval.

Approved extensions may be added where necessary without affecting the standard structure.

---

### TUR-03 — Consistent Terminology

All objectives shall use the approved engineering terminology and naming standards adopted by the AVIA repository.

---

### TUR-04 — Completeness

All mandatory fields shall be completed before an objective enters the engineering review process.

Optional fields may be omitted only when they are not applicable.

---

### TUR-05 — Governance Compliance

Every objective created using this template shall comply with the requirements established in:

- OBJECTIVE_GOVERNANCE.md
- System Objective Specification (SOS)

---

### TUR-06 — Controlled Modification

Changes to this template shall be made only through the approved governance and change management process.

Existing objective documents shall remain traceable to the template version from which they were created.

---

### TUR-07 — Repository Consistency

The template shall be used consistently across all objective categories to preserve uniformity throughout the AVIA objective library.
